"""Côte d'Ivoire — The Abidjan Transit Ledger (self-contained submission).

One text router over ten query-template labels (five old, five new). The
trained model is a TF-IDF (words + word pairs, sublinear tf, l2 norm) over
1237 features followed by multinomial logistic regression (10 classes),
trained with replay on old and new examples together (5-fold CV: old 1.000,
new 0.992, min per fold 0.960; both gates are 0.85).

Everything needed for inference is embedded below as plain literals, so this
file has no runtime dependencies: no checkpoints, no pickle, no numpy, no
scikit-learn. The math reproduces scikit-learn exactly:
  tf  = 1 + ln(count)                (sublinear_tf)
  idf = ln((1+n)/(1+df)) + 1         (smooth_idf)
  vector = tf*idf, then l2-normalised (zero vectors stay zero)
  label = argmax_k(vector . coef_k + intercept_k)

I/O contract: reads test-input.json from the current directory (list of
{"id", "text"} records), writes predictions.json (list of {"id", "label"}).
"""
